 "case:hints.h_accuse.levels.2": "The killer is Fiona Brodie: she never left Nightjar’s floor after six, and struck him with the award, to stop Will telling Halcyon what Joel had found. Prove it with your answer about the bench, your answer about who was in the Nest, and your answer about what Joel found.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.0": "For each proof slot, ask: which card shows it wasn’t Joel, which shows who was with Will when he died, and which shows what Will was about to do?",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.1": "Why it wasn’t Joel: your answer about the bench, or his watch file. The opportunity: your answers about the Nest or Will’s light, the New York call, or what Fiona admitted. The motive: your answer about what Joel found, Growth Partners’ report, Gavin’s messages, Kai’s admission, or ‘Night traffic’.",
 "case:hints.h_accuse_ready.levels.2": "Accuse Fiona Brodie: she never left Nightjar’s floor after six, and struck him with the award, to stop Will telling Halcyon what Joel had found. Prove it with your answer about the bench, your answer about who was in the Nest, and your answer about what Joel found.",
 "case:hints.h_bench.levels.0": "The police say GPS can’t tell the bench from the bike-store door. What else did Joel’s watch measure?",
