 "case:locations.hall.description": "Inside the street door is a hall of black and white stone flags. A corridor at the back on the left runs to the bike store. A small lift and a stone staircase climb to the top of the house, and the building manager’s desk sits under the stairs, unstaffed after five.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_hall_book.label": "The visitor book",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_hall_book.text": "On the building manager’s desk, Thursday’s page: ‘Gavin Rourke · Larchwood Ventures · for Nightjar · in 16:28 · out 18:24.’ Nobody else signed in after lunch.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_hall_intercom.label": "The intercom screen",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_hall_intercom.text": "A small screen beside the street door lists the intercom’s calls, each with a still from its camera.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_hall_stairs.label": "The stairs and the lift",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_hall_stairs.text": "Sixty-four stone stairs climb round the walls to Nightjar’s floor, fourteen metres up, with a small lift beside them. Both come out at the east end of the floor, beside Will’s office. The bike-store corridor joins the foot of the stairs.",
 "case:locations.hall.name": "The hall at No. 31",
 "case:locations.hall.summary": "The intercom screen, the visitor book, and the stairs and lift up to Nightjar.",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.0.label": "The Nest",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.1.label": "Desks",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.2.label": "The Fishbowl",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.3.label": "Printer",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.4.label": "Kitchen",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.5.label": "Will’s office",
 "case:locations.office.art.props.6.label": "Stairs and lift",
 "case:locations.office.description": "The top of No. 31 is one long room under a sloping ceiling: rows of desks with plants and headphones, a glass meeting room in the middle that everyone calls the Fishbowl, and a kitchen at the back. The Nest is at the west end, and Will’s corner office is at the east end, by the stairs and the lift. The ceiling lights come on by themselves as you walk under them, a bank at a time. Most of the team are working from home this week.",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_fishbowl.label": "The Fishbowl",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_fishbowl.text": "The glass meeting room where Joel and Will rowed on Thursday. From every desk on the floor you can see straight in. Someone has wiped the whiteboard, but in one corner, in Joel’s square capitals, a scrap survives: ‘03:00:00’.",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_joel.label": "Joel’s desk",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_joel.text": "The police have his laptop. They’ve left a mug that says IT WORKS ON MY MACHINE, a jar of energy gels and his marathon plan, pinned to the partition: ‘THU: run home. Harbour loop, back through Queen Sq, then home. 10 km easy.’ The London Marathon, on 26 April, is circled. Underneath: ‘sub-3??’",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_nest.label": "The Nest",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_nest.text": "A small room at the west end of the floor, as far from the stairs and the lift as you can get. Beside its frosted-glass door is a booking screen.",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_printer.label": "The printer",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_printer.text": "The office printer by the kitchen door. Its tray is full of Halcyon’s contract drafts, and underneath them is something else.",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_will.label": "Will’s office",
 "case:locations.office.hotspots.hs_off_will.text": "The blinds are down, as they were on Thursday night. The police took his laptop and his phone, and left the rest: a cold pizza box, a pen, his reading glasses. There’s no sign of the pages Joel gave him. On the shelf by the door, a clean square in the dust shows where the award stood. Unlike the sensor lights out on the floor, his office light works from a switch by the door. His running medals hang on the back of the door, beside a photo of Will and Joel at the finish of last year’s Bristol Half, arm in arm and soaked.",
 "case:locations.office.name": "Nightjar’s floor",
 "case:locations.office.summary": "The Nest, the Fishbowl, the printer, Joel’s desk and Will’s office.",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.0.label": "No. 31",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.1.label": "Bike store",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.10.label": "To the harbour",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.3.label": "Street door",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.4.label": "North path",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.5.label": "Bench",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.6.label": "Lawns",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.7.label": "King William",
 "case:locations.square.art.props.8.label": "Plane trees",
 "case:locations.square.description": "Queen Square on a damp Tuesday evening: lawns and gravel paths under bare plane trees, with King William III on horseback in the middle. Offices stand on all four sides, their windows going dark one by one. No. 31 is on the north side, a tall house of pale stone, and Nightjar’s lights are still on at the top.",
 "case:locations.square.hotspots.hs_sq_bench.label": "Joel’s bench",
 "case:locations.square.hotspots.hs_sq_bench.text": "You sit where Joel sat on Thursday night, in the drizzle.",
 "case:locations.square.hotspots.hs_sq_bikestore.label": "The bike-store door",
 "case:locations.square.hotspots.hs_sq_bikestore.text": "A plain door in No. 31’s side wall, with a keypad. Fiona gives you the code: everyone at Nightjar knows it. Behind it, past the bikes and the showers, a corridor leads to the foot of the stairs. Nothing records who uses it, and there’s no camera.",
 "case:locations.square.hotspots.hs_sq_door.label": "The street door",
 "case:locations.square.hotspots.hs_sq_door.text": "A black door with a fanlight and a brass intercom panel. Nightjar is the top button. A small camera lens looks out above the buttons. It takes a picture only when somebody presses one.",
 "case:locations.square.name": "Queen Square",
 "case:locations.square.summary": "Joel’s bench, King William, and No. 31’s street door and bike-store door.",
 "case:setting": "Queen Square · Bristol · March 2026",
 "case:sketchCredit": "SKETCH: SITE VISIT, 10 MARCH 2026 · NOT TO SCALE",
 "case:sketchTitle": "QUEEN SQUARE",
 "case:stayLabel": "Stay in Queen Square",
 "case:tagline": "He ran ten kilometres in fifty minutes. His run took sixty-five.",
 "case:timeline.conclusion": "The row was at ten past six, and at 18:34 somebody went into the Nest and shut the door. Joel set off at 20:56, Gavin was turned away at the door at 21:06, and Will messaged Claire at 21:20. Joel sat down on his bench at 21:24. Just after half past nine the lights came on along the floor, from the Nest towards Will’s office. At 21:34 Will’s heart stopped, and at 21:36 his light went off. A dead man doesn’t switch off his light.",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_bench.text": "Joel sits down on the bench",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_bench.time": "21:24",
 "case:timeline.events.tl_dark.teaser": "Something else somebody saw.",
